    {
      "id": "CVE-2026-111056",
      "publishedDate": "2026-10-19T16:00:57.576Z",
      "lastModifiedDate": "2026-10-19T16:00:57.576Z",
      "description": "FOSSBilling is an open source billing and client-management platform. From 0.1.0 until 0.8.7, the unauthenticated POST /api/guest/client/create endpoint reveals whether a submitted email belongs to a registered client because guest signup returns a distinct unredacted error when the submitted email already exists. The trigger is an unauthenticated request to POST /api/guest/client/create with a target email address. An attacker can compare the guest-signup response for a target email to determine whether the email belongs to an existing FOSSBilling client. Box\\Mod\\Client\\Api\\Guest::create returns the error after Client\\Service::clientAlreadyExists finds a matching record, and the API response exposes that exception message without redaction. This issue is fixed in version 0.8.7.",
      "severity": "8.5",
      "fix_suggestion": "📦 受影响组件：FOSSBilling FOSSBilling\n🔓 漏洞类型：Exposure of Sensitive Information, CWE-204, CWE-307 (CWE-200, CWE-204, CWE-307)\n📊 官方评级：HIGH (CVSS 8.5)\n🛠️ 修复建议：\n1. 确认受影响的版本范围（见上方 Affected Products）\n2. 升级到厂商官方发布的最稳定安全版本\n3. 检查官方安全公告获取补丁链接\n4. 如无法立即升级，实施临时缓解措施：\n   - 网络层：WAF 规则 / IPS 签名 / 零信任策略\n   - 主机层：最小化暴露面 / 禁用危险功能 / 输入过滤\n5. 修复后使用 NVD / 厂商 PoC 验证修复有效性",
